WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.868
- How does it feel to be the vet?

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.204
- Man, it's crazy cuz—

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:04.804
I don't think

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.508
I haven't talked about this yet—
but it's crazy because, like, whenever music—

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:13.546
like, we listen to music at practice
and even when we in our layup lines in a game,

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.215
and it be certain songs that come on

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.384
and I'll always ask the guys, like,
"You know who this is?"

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.421
They be like, "I never heard this song
in my life," and it could be like a Mary J.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.489
Blige song or something.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:26.860
You know what I mean?
- Yeah.
- It could be a song from 2005, and they have no clue.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.461
- Like, I was just born.
- Yeah.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:33.233
And it's like, "I was born in 2001,"
and it's like, "Oh, my God."

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:37.570
But at the same time,
you know, it's enjoyable

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.641
cuz you learn so much from 'em,
and they teach you so much

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:45.078
in the same token, and once you, like,

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.380
accept that, it's fun.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.084
You know, I think one of the guys one day
in practice was like, "Man, you're the only

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.020
person on the team born in the '80s.
What does it feel like?" And I'm like,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.123
"I'm born in '89. I'm only 32."

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.360
You know what I mean? It's just crazy

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.496
to have that back and forth.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.297
And we have fun with it.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.200
So it's definitely cool
just to, just to have that

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.803
because I learn so much
from those guys as well.
- Yeah.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.572
Born in the '80s. In '89.
- Yeah.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.142
That's crazy.
- And what music they tried to put you on? Like,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.145
NBA YoungBoy or somethin'?
- Everything. You name it. It be some people.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:23.483
But, but even that.
I listen to it. Like, "Who hot right now?"

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.451
I listen to it

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.820
just so I could be on the same page
as them as well, you know what I mean?
- Yeah.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.222
- So it'd be cool.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:33.026
- So when did you realize you were the vet?
Was it when they were like, "'89"?

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.662
- Yeah, I think it was like training camp.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.032
It was, it was some somewhere around there.
I think we was listening to, like,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.735
50 Cent "Get Rich or Die Tryin'."

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:46.539
And somebody was like, "Yeah,
I was like one years old or two years old."

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.907
And I was like, I remember

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.878
buying that CD, you know what I mean?
- That was all anybody cared about.
- Yeah.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:56.116
I remember going to the store buying that.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:59.719
And that was the moment.
That was my first moment.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.021
I was like,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.223
it's going to be a long year.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.458
- Oh, yeah. You got to get them
on all that stuff.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.694
They probably haven't heard
even like old Wayne.

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.930
It's so much. I asked them about Jay-Z.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.967
They was like, "Yeah, I heard about two or
three Jay-Z songs." And I'm like,

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.769
I feel offended.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.339
You know? I feel offended.
- Yeah.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.308
Oh, no. My gosh, no.
Then you have some teaching to do. Cuz this is real life lessons.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:26.913
- I do. I do. In their credit,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.516
they, they listen.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.751
You know, whatever
it is. Not even just music.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:35.221
Just anything in general. Even with movies.
Like, I do the same thing with movies.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:39.325
Have you seen this movie, this movie?
And a lot of them—like, it was one guy.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.662
I'll say his name: Patrick Williams.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.731
I made a reference.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.699
One game we was playing,
I made a reference

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.069
from "300," the movie "300,"
and he didn't get it.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:54.807
I was like, "You know what '300' is?"
He said, "No." I said, "It's a movie." He said, "What?"

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.810
He said, "Man, I'mma go home
and watch it tonight." So he went home.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.181
Watched it. Called me after the movie and said,
"Oh, my God, the movie was amazing.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.284
You got another movie for me?"
You know what I mean?
- Oh, that's great.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.519
What did you say, like,
"This is Sparta"?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.855
- Yeah. It was crazy. It was great. But

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.391
he went to go watch it and he, you know, but—
 - That's great.

